message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "Observational Aliasing Bounds Generalization in Constrained Active-Sensing Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning"
version: v1.0-icet2026
# LICENSE lists the software file-sets under MIT and the data and records
# under CC BY 4.0. Its software file-sets include instruments/ and scripts/.
# CFF 1.2.0 reads a list of licenses as alternatives, so this field names
# only MIT.
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  This repository holds the code, grading instruments, run provenance,
  per-checkpoint grade records, the 27 graded policy checkpoints, and a
  claim-to-source traceability register that accompany the IEEE ICET 2026 paper
  of the same title. All four authors share
  the affiliation: School of Computing Sciences, Pak-Austria Fachhochschule
  Institute of Applied Sciences and Technology, Haripur, Pakistan.

# Only the CORRESPONDING author's address appears here. The other three are
# student roll-number addresses tied to enrollment.
# The corresponding author is Musadaq Mansoor. On page 1 of the paper, an asterisk
# follows the name and a footnote reads "*Corresponding author."
#
# ORCID identifiers are OMITTED. This file is valid
# without them, and each can later be added as one `orcid:` line under the
# relevant author without restructuring anything.
